# Set maximum contact torques of the robot's joint motion controller. The controller regulates its
# output to keep contact torques with the environment under these values. Requires the driver to run
# with rdk_control_mode:=joint_impedance.
#
# max_contact_torques must hold one entry per joint of the hardware component, in URDF order. An
# invalid request is rejected as a whole and nothing changes.

# Maximum contact torque, one entry per joint in URDF order. Valid range [0, tau_max]. Raising this
# increases the force the robot may exert on its surroundings. [Nm]
float64[] max_contact_torques
---
bool success

# Operator-facing explanation of the outcome, naming the joint and the bound on a rejection
string message

# The values now held by the driver, unchanged from before on a rejection
MaxContactTorque setting
